From 58d407383095ec34c3ad0d97002707235844b569 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viswanath Kraleti <viswanath.kraleti@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 17:12:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] linux-firmware: backport shikra wlan firmware support

The current linux-firmware 20260910 version doesn't include the WLAN
firmware required by Shikra platforms. Backport the upstream commit
f64d7db7d264 ("ath10k: WCN3990: hw1.0: add shikra firmware files") to
ensure the required WCN3990 Shikra firmware files are picked up to
enable WLAN functionality on Shikra boards.

The patch can be dropped once OE-Core updates linux-firmware to a
release that includes commit f64d7db7d264.

Signed-off-by: Viswanath Kraleti <viswanath.kraleti@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://gitlab.com/kernel-firmware/linux-firmware/-/commit/f64d7db7d2646e1c7744963d540524f523ae0443]
---
 ...3990-hw1.0-add-shikra-firmware-files.patch | 40814 ++++++++++++++++
 .../linux-firmware/linux-firmware_20260910.bb |     5 +-
 2 files changed, 40818 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 meta/recipes-kernel/linux-firmware/linux-firmware/0001-ath10k-WCN3990-hw1.0-add-shikra-firmware-files.patch

